Keeps this directory in git.

Dockerfile.production does `COPY patches/ ./patches/` before `pnpm install`,
because pnpm hashes a patched dependency's file during RESOLUTION — a declared
patch that is not in the image kills the install with ENOENT, exit 254.

The directory therefore has to exist even when nothing is patched: with the
last patch deleted (its change went upstream in @hanzo/ui 8.0.76) the COPY
failed in four seconds on a missing path, and no image was cut.

Delete this file only together with that COPY.
